msgid "Noise Modeling {#noise-modeling}"
msgstr "Noise Modeling {#noise-modeling}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A noise model describes how errors affect the results from executing a quantum circuit. Noise models support several stages of a typical workflow including: simulating a circuit classically to estimate expected performance before submitting a job  or to inform an error-mitigation technique such as probabilistic error cancellation. For general strategies to reduce the impact of noise during execution, see [Overview of noise management techniques](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques).\n"
msgstr "Inilalarawan ng noise model kung paano nakakaapekto ang mga error sa mga result mula sa pag-execute ng quantum circuit. Sinusuportahan ng mga noise model ang ilang yugto ng karaniwang workflow kabilang ang: pag-simulate ng circuit nang classical para tantiyahin ang inaasahang performance bago magsumite ng job o para gabayan ang error-mitigation technique tulad ng probabilistic error cancellation. Para sa mga pangkalahatang estratehiya para mabawasan ang epekto ng noise habang nag-e-execute, tingnan ang [Pangkalahatang-ideya ng mga noise management technique](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This page collects the packages and capabilities that support each part of that workflow, grouped into learning noise from a device, building a noise model for classical simulation, and refining a noise model for a specific error-mitigation technique.\n"
msgstr "Kinokolekta ng page na ito ang mga package at kakayahan na sumusuporta sa bawat bahagi ng workflow na iyon, na nakapangkat sa pag-learn ng noise mula sa device, pagbuo ng noise model para sa classical simulation, at pag-refine ng noise model para sa partikular na error-mitigation technique.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Building and running noise learning algorithms {#building-and-running-noise-learning-algorithms}"
msgstr "Pagbuo at pagpapatakbo ng mga noise learning algorithm {#building-and-running-noise-learning-algorithms}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use noise learning packages to characterize a device's noise directly from experimental data. These packages run randomized circuits to estimate error rates and build a noise model that reflects actual hardware behavior.\n"
msgstr "Gumamit ng mga noise learning package para i-characterize ang noise ng device direkta mula sa experimental data. Nagpapatakbo ang mga package na ito ng mga randomized circuit para tantiyahin ang mga error rate at bumuo ng noise model na sumasalamin sa aktwal na gawi ng hardware.\n"

